📈 Advantages of MLP

✔ Can learn complex patterns
✔ Works for both classification & regression
✔ Flexible architecture
✔ Foundation of deep learning

---

❌ Limitations of MLP

❌ Requires large data
❌ Prone to overfitting
❌ Not suitable for spatial data (images)
❌ Not good for sequential data

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📊 MLP vs Other Neural Networks

| Model    | Best For                |
| -------- | ----------------------- |
| MLP      | Structured/tabular data |
| CNN      | Images                  |
| RNN/LSTM | Sequential data         |
| GAN      | Data generation         |

---

🧠 When to Use MLP?

Use MLP when:

✔ Data is structured (tabular)
✔ Features are independent
✔ Problem is classification/regression

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Too many layers → overfitting
❌ Not normalizing data
❌ Wrong activation function
❌ Wrong loss function

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Best Practices

✔ Normalize input data
✔ Use ReLU in hidden layers
✔ Use dropout for regularization
✔ Tune number of layers
✔ Use early stopping

